
<section class="phase-page testing-page">

    <h1>Test Design</h1>

    <p class="page-intro">
        In this phase, I designed manual test cases for selected
        functionalities of the Automation Exercise website.
        The identified test conditions were converted into
        structured test cases with test data, steps, and
        expected results.
    </p>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Design Approach</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Positive Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Designed scenarios using valid inputs
                    to verify expected system behavior,
                    such as successful login and product search.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Negative Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Designed scenarios using invalid or
                    unexpected inputs, such as duplicate
                    emails and invalid email formats.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Scenario-Based Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Designed test cases around user actions,
                    including product selection, cart quantity,
                    logout, and product removal.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Case Structure</h2>

        <p>
            Each test case was documented using a consistent
            structure to make execution and reporting easier.
        </p>

        <ul class="goals-list">
            <li>Test Case ID and Title</li>
            <li>Feature</li>
            <li>Preconditions</li>
            <li>Test Data</li>
            <li>Test Steps</li>
            <li>Expected Result</li>
            <li>Actual Result</li>
            <li>Execution Status</li>
            <li>Notes and Evidence</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Case Coverage</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>4 Test Cases</h3>
                <p>User Registration</p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>2 Test Cases</h3>
                <p>User Authentication</p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>3 Test Cases</h3>
                <p>Product Search</p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>4 Test Cases</h3>
                <p>Shopping Cart</p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Designed Test Cases</h2>

        <p>
            The following table summarizes the 13 documented
            manual test cases and their expected behavior.
            Execution results are presented separately
            in the Test Execution phase.
        </p>

        <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="test-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Test Case ID</th>
                        <th>Test Scenario</th>
                        <th>Test Data / Condition</th>
                        <th>Expected Result</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>

                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-REG-001</td>
                        <td>Required field validation</td>
                        <td>Leave a required field empty</td>
                        <td>Registration is blocked and the missing field is indicated.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-REG-002</td>
                        <td>Mobile number validation</td>
                        <td>Letters and digits in mobile number</td>
                        <td>Check input behavior against the confirmed phone validation requirements.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-REG-003</td>
                        <td>Duplicate email registration</td>
                        <td>Previously registered email</td>
                        <td>Registration is rejected with an appropriate message.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-REG-004</td>
                        <td>Invalid email format</td>
                        <td>Email without &#64; symbol</td>
                        <td>Invalid email format is rejected.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-LOGIN-001</td>
                        <td>Valid login</td>
                        <td>Valid registered credentials</td>
                        <td>User logs in and their username is displayed.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-LOGOUT-001</td>
                        <td>Logout and session check</td>
                        <td>Logout, Back, and Refresh</td>
                        <td>The logged-out session is not restored.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-SEARCH-001</td>
                        <td>Existing product search</td>
                        <td>Blue Top</td>
                        <td>The matching product appears in results.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-SEARCH-002</td>
                        <td>Non-existent product search</td>
                        <td>zznotfound987654</td>
                        <td>No unrelated products appear as matches.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-SEARCH-003</td>
                        <td>Partial product search</td>
                        <td>Blue</td>
                        <td>Matching partial-name products appear, if partial search is supported.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-CART-001</td>
                        <td>Add a single product</td>
                        <td>Blue Top, quantity 1</td>
                        <td>Correct product, quantity, and price appear in the cart.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-CART-002</td>
                        <td>Set product quantity</td>
                        <td>Blue Top, quantity 4</td>
                        <td>Quantity is 4 and the total equals unit price multiplied by 4.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-CART-003</td>
                        <td>Add the same product twice</td>
                        <td>Blue Top added twice</td>
                        <td>The cart represents two units with the correct total.</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>TC-CART-004</td>
                        <td>Remove product and refresh</td>
                        <td>Remove Blue Top, then Refresh</td>
                        <td>The product remains removed after refreshing.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Design Deliverable</h2>

        <p>
            A Microsoft Excel test case workbook was prepared
            to document the 13 manual test cases, including
            preconditions, test data, execution steps,
            expected results, actual results, status,
            and review notes.
        </p>

        <p>
            Some registration validation conditions require
            additional requirement confirmation.
            These are documented for review rather than
            being classified as confirmed defects.
        </p>
    </section>

</section>
